# This repository holds a Python distribution, so unlike the sibling document
# repositories the build artefacts below are not hypothetical -- they appear the
# first time anyone runs `uv build` or installs the package editable.
#
# `dist/` and `build/` are anchored at the root deliberately, and the
# `*.egg-info` rule is NOT anchored. In the monorepo this package came from, the
# ignore rule was written as `packages/*/build/` and `dist/` was not ignored at
# all -- so a stale `build/lib/` tree and a built wheel both sat untracked and
# un-ignored in the working tree, one `cp -r` away from being published. A rule
# that only covers the layout you had is not a rule.
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.whl
*.tar.gz

# Byte cache and test/tooling state.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Virtual environments. `uv run --no-project` avoids creating one, and the README
# says why; this is the safety net for the invocation that forgets.
.venv/
venv/

# Environment and key material. Nothing here needs credentials, which is exactly
# when this is cheap to add: a key committed once is compromised even after the
# file is deleted, so the rule has to predate the key rather than follow it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa
id_ed25519
keys.txt

# Local agent configuration. Deliberately untracked: settings files here
# accumulate machine-specific absolute paths and permission allowlists, which are
# a property of one workstation rather than of this project.
.claude/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
